  "_the_lavender_rim_band_is_a_RIM_ADMISSION_not_a_material": "It IS exported (canon puts it in allowed_bands, which palette_gate.py reads - unlike the dragon's suspended blue-violet stratum, which canon deliberately keeps in a key the gate does not read). E14 Ruling 17c admitted it so the gate's numbers mean something on accepted work: the realised backdrop sits at C* 32.6-37.1, far above the floor, so its antialiased rim mixing is a real above-floor hue population INSIDE the silhouette. It covers NO declared material - 92.8% of its support is rim pixels at median depth 1.00 px, against wine at 8.0% and gold at 0.3%. The blindness it buys (interior backdrop-family arrivals, and a DRIFTED declared material - the gem did exactly that at seed 770701) is watched by the standing DEPTH diagnostic, not by hue.",
